 Keeping W3-W4-W5 pairs gives me flexibility for multiple chow formations\n- B5-B6-B7 has excellent potential with 4 copies of each still unshown\n\nReason: T6 is the most isolated tile in my hand with the least synergy. It doesn't connect with my W3-W5 pairs or my B5-B7 holdings. With only 2 T6 tiles remaining unshown, its potential is limited. Discarding it allows me to focus on developing either the Character (W) or Dot (B) sequences, both of which have better completion potential.\n\nAnswer: Play T6"}
